    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 224</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 05 May 2025 15:15:46 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;1 x, _:= f()&#xA;2 x,_ = f()&#xA;3 x, y := f()&#xA;4 x, y = f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#xA;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
