    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 145</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Dec 2024 12:34:35 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_145/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. var str string&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A, D&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Only &lt;code&gt;var&lt;/code&gt; can be used for global definitions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;B: Only supports local variable declaration.&#xA;C: Assignment, not definition.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 131</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_131/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Dec 2024 11:59:22 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_131/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding channels, which of the following syntax is correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. var ch chan int&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. ch := make(chan int)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. &amp;lt;- ch&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D. ch &amp;lt;-&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A, B, C&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A declares variable &lt;code&gt;ch&lt;/code&gt; of type &lt;code&gt;chan int&lt;/code&gt;, but does not initialize it.&#xA;B declares variable &lt;code&gt;ch&lt;/code&gt; of type &lt;code&gt;chan int&lt;/code&gt;, and initializes it.&#xA;C reads from the channel, discarding the value.&#xA;D is incorrect; writing to a channel requires a value.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
