    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 085</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_085/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:11 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_085/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following options is correct?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    if a := 1; false {&#xA;    } else if b := 2; false {&#xA;    } else {&#xA;        println(a, b)&#xA;    }&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. 1 2&#xA;B. compilation error&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Involves code block issues.&#xA;For details, you can refer to this article:&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://studygolang.com/articles/35587&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;https://studygolang.com/articles/35587&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;After expanding, the code becomes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;{&#xA;        a := 1&#xA;        if false {&#xA;&#xA;        } else {&#xA;            b := 2&#xA;            if false {&#xA;&#xA;            } else {&#xA;                println(a, b)&#xA;            }&#xA;        }&#xA;    }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 070</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:53 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;x, &lt;em&gt;:= f()&#xA;x,&lt;/em&gt; = f()&#xA;x, y := f()&#xA;x, y = f()&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#xA;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 053</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:33 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_053/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To define a package-level global string variable, which of the following syntax is correct (multiple choice):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A. var str string&#xA;B. str := &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#xA;C. str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&#xA;D. var str = &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A, D&#xA;The key is &amp;ldquo;package-level global&amp;rdquo;.&#xA;B: &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; can only be used inside functions.&#xA;C: This is an assignment, not a declaration.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 039</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:16 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding channels, which of the following syntax is correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;A. var ch chan int&#xA;B. ch := make(chan int)&#xA;C. &amp;lt;- ch&#xA;D. ch &amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: ABC&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A and B both declare a channel; C reads from a channel;&#xA;Writing to a channel must include a value, so D is incorrect.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 022</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_022/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 19:49:56 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_022/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile? If so, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;var(&#xA;    size := 1024&#xA;    max_size = size*2&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    fmt.Println(size,max_size)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: No.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var(&#xA;    size := 1024&#xA;)&#xA;Does not conform to specification.&#xA;Problem 1: `var` variable declaration cannot use `:=`.&#xA;Problem 2: `:=` can only be used inside a function; this problem uses it for declaring global variables.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reference Analysis: The main point of this problem is the short variable declaration mode, such as: &lt;code&gt;x := 100&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
